WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.401
-The president participated

00:00:02.401 --> 00:00:03.903
in an ABC town hall

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.538
with undecided voters
last night,

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.840
where he lied
as often as he breathed.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.376
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:14.547 line:0%
[ Suspenseful theme plays ]

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:17.483
ABC invited Trump to a primetime
town hall last night,

00:00:17.483 --> 00:00:19.518
for some reason and,
honestly, I'm

00:00:19.518 --> 00:00:22.522
not sure I see the value
in hosting an event like this.

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:23.723
We know what he's gonna say.

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:25.057
He's gonna repeat

00:00:25.057 --> 00:00:27.560
the same deranged lies
we've heard a million times.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.897
The only TV show it would be
worth having Trump on

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:32.999
is "Ellen's Game of Games."

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.901
Then, at least,
we could see him lie

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:37.036
and drop into a pool full
of jelly beans

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:39.305
or get sprayed with a hose
full of chocolate sauce.

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:40.673
Of course, you know,
that's probably --

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:41.807
probably what he wants.

00:00:41.807 --> 00:00:43.242
[ As Trump ]
Oh, no, not the

00:00:43.242 --> 00:00:44.844
chocolate sauce hose.

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:46.346
Really, the best
you can hope for,

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:47.647
with a town hall like this,

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:50.483
is a new lie
for reporters to debunk.

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:53.153
[ As Trump ]
You know, they say
coronavirus can be cured

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:56.556
by swallowing a golf ball
covered in Emergen-C

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.991
while shining a laser
pointer up your butt.

00:00:58.991 --> 00:01:01.293
And then, the reporters say,
"Oh, that's a new one!

00:01:01.293 --> 00:01:02.728
Quick, someone fact-check that!

00:01:02.728 --> 00:01:04.330
This one's gonna get us
the Pulitzer."

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:08.501
Although, I will say the one
genuinely valuable service,

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:09.602
with a town hall like this,

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:12.271
is watching normal
people interact

00:01:12.271 --> 00:01:13.639
with a nutjob like Trump.

00:01:13.639 --> 00:01:16.275
Anchors and reporters,
they all adhere

00:01:16.275 --> 00:01:18.444
to a certain level
of decorum and tradition,

00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:21.280
even though Trump is
an obvious crazy person,

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.715
but normal people
react differently

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.650
because they've had
experience with it.

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:27.553
When you ride the bus or the
subway to work every day,

00:01:27.553 --> 00:01:30.390
you interact with your
fair share of Trumps.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:33.492
Most people just ignore
the dude on the subway yellin'

00:01:33.492 --> 00:01:35.995
about mind control cockroaches
stealing our cigarettes.

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:39.198
But if Wolf Blitzer
ever rode the F train,

00:01:39.198 --> 00:01:40.432
he would have to say...

00:01:40.432 --> 00:01:41.968
[ As Blitzer ]
Sir, what's your proof of that?

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:44.237
I'm sorry.
We're out of time.

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:45.638
We'll have to leave it there.

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:47.874
Case in point, last night,
a voter asked Trump

00:01:47.874 --> 00:01:50.376
about his repeated attempts
to repeal Obamacare

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:53.479
and do away with its protections
for preexisting conditions,

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:55.547
including a lawsuit

00:01:55.547 --> 00:01:57.884
his administration has filed
with the Supreme Court,

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.485
and, when Trump tried
to interrupt her,

00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:01.887
she asked him to let her finish.

00:02:01.887 --> 00:02:05.457 line:0%
-Should preexisting conditions,

00:02:05.457 --> 00:02:08.460 line:0%
which Obamacare brought into --

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.697 line:0%
brought to fruition, be removed

00:02:11.697 --> 00:02:12.865 line:0%
-No.
-without --

00:02:12.865 --> 00:02:15.802 line:0%
Please stop and let me
finish my question, sir.

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:17.437
-Oh, it's so cathartic
to see someone

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:18.804
put Trump in his place
like that.

00:02:18.804 --> 00:02:21.374
Can we please let her
moderate all three debates,

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:23.609
and can we hold them
in middle school, so,

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:25.611
every time Trump
gets reprimanded like that,

00:02:25.611 --> 00:02:28.881
he has to sit in the corner,
facing the wall?

00:02:28.881 --> 00:02:30.616
That's what happens
when Trump steps

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:32.284
outside his
right-wing media bubble.

00:02:32.284 --> 00:02:33.987
Most of the time,
he surrounds himself

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:35.421
with sycophants and yes-men,

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:38.625
so he's rarely treated like
the idiot blowhard he is.

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:40.225
Fox News hosts
don't interrupt Trump

00:02:40.225 --> 00:02:41.794
when he calls in
to "Fox &amp; Friends"

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:43.228
and rambles for an hour.

00:02:43.228 --> 00:02:44.931 line:0%
The hosts just sit there,

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:46.298 line:0%
staring blankly into the camera,

00:02:46.298 --> 00:02:48.300 line:0%
like they're posing
for passport photos.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:49.936 line:0%
They look like those

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:51.637
out-of-town tourists
in Times Square,

00:02:51.637 --> 00:02:54.940
watching Elmo drop his pants
and take a dump on the sidewalk.

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:57.476
In fact, Fox News is apparently
so shocked and disturbed

00:02:57.476 --> 00:03:00.246
by the idea of Trump
answering questions from voters

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:03.282
that Laura Ingraham played
a montage of those questions

00:03:03.282 --> 00:03:04.384 line:0%
with the lower-third...

00:03:08.854 --> 00:03:12.058
Man, they just never, ever stop
making excuses for him.

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:16.095
Look, it's not a "gotcha" book
when Bob Woodward tells you

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:18.363
he's recording
the interview for a book

00:03:18.363 --> 00:03:19.899
and it's not an ambush

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:23.836
if you're invited to participate
in a town hall and you say yes.

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:26.372
When Washington wanted
to ambush the Hessians,

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:28.174
he crossed the Delaware River
secretly,

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:29.842
